# x = a: eq_2_2 with (a, 0) in place of y. Equality is symmetric, so there is no eq_1_2.
kernel:        eq_2_1
input:         x = x0 x1
input:         a
output:        mask m
value:         x-a
requires:      canonical x
ensures:       predicate m eq x a
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/Compare.v eq_2_1_correct
source:        limbs compared in order (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; the non-finite layer tests the operands

h = eq(x0, a)
l = eq(x1, 0)
m = and(h, l)
